# ============================================================================
#  DO NOT PUT A REAL KEY IN THIS FILE.
#
#  Git tracks this one, and this repository is public. A key written here
#  would be published the moment anything is committed, and a closed pull
#  request stays readable, so it could not reliably be taken back.
#
#  The real key goes in a file called .env, which git ignores.
# ============================================================================
#
# The extraction step calls a model, and the model needs a key. The key is free,
# from Google AI Studio, and it is only needed to run the extraction by hand.
# Every test in this project runs without one.
#
# To set it up:
#
#   1. Make a new file called .env in this same folder, with the leading dot.
#   2. Put one line in it, with the key after the equals sign, no spaces around
#      the equals sign and no quotation marks:
#
#          GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here
#
# Type it into an editor, never into a terminal. A key typed at a PowerShell
# prompt is written in clear text into that shell's saved history and stays
# there, because the filter meant to catch sensitive commands does not match a
# name with underscores in it. See ADR-0035.
#
# Leave the line below empty. It is here to name the setting, nothing else.

GEMINI_API_KEY=